==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 2~20 seconds<sup>60f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Wall Doge]]s spawn, delay 2~20 seconds<sup>60f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**1 [[Doge]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 4~20 seconds<sup>120f~600f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn, delay 4~20 seconds<sup>120f~600f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Wall Doge]]s spawn, delay 4~20 seconds<sup>120f~600f</sup>.
**1 [[Hyper Mr. (Enemy)|Hyper Mr.]] spawns.
**1 [[Heavenly Hippoe]] spawns.
**1 [[Angelic Gory]] spawns.
**1 [[Wall Doge]] spawns.
**Infinite [[Hyper Mr. (Enemy)|Hyper Messrs.]] spawn, delay 80~80.67 seconds<sup>2,400f~2,420f</sup>.
**1 [[Heavenly Hippoe]] spawns.
**1 [[Angelic Gory]] spawns.
**Infinite [[Hyper Mr. (Enemy)|Hyper Messrs.]] spawn, delay 53.33~54 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,620f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The most optimal way to beat this stage is to use backline Area Attackers to kill the Hyper Messrs before they are able to stack up and shred your entire army. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] and [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] are perfect for this job, as both have high range and do good enough damage to quickly wipe out the Hyper Messrs. The supporting Angel peons can be stalled easily if you happen to own [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]], but stalling them with your usual [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Tank]] and [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] combo should be enough. This stage is primarily a DPS check, so you should bring out all the stops to kill the enemies as quickly as possible; [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] should be considered to speed up the process.

